  ],
  "text": "The yellow was in the leaf all summer. Green was just louder. Autumn looks like paint going on. It is actually paint coming off. Chlorophyll is the green, and it is expensive for a tree to make. As the days shorten, the tree starts taking it back rather than wasting it. What is left underneath was there the whole time. Yellow and orange, uncovered. Red is different. Red is made fresh, on purpose, in autumn. Nobody is certain why. Sunscreen for the withdrawal is the best guess we have. Because the whole thing is a tree emptying its pockets before it lets go. Autumn is not decoration. It is a withdrawal, and the colour is what is left behind. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
